WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.200
Child Benefit: £27.05 a week for the eldest or only child and £17.90 for each additional child. It depends on your immigration status: check before you claim.

2
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:28.200
If one parent earns over £60,000 a year, part of it is paid back through tax; above £80,000, all of it. Free childcare for working families (England): up to 30 hours a week, 38 weeks a year, for children from 9 months to 4 years old.

3
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:40.000
Each parent must earn a minimum (for example, about £203 a week if aged 21 or over) and you must reconfirm every 3 months.

4
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Tax-Free Childcare: for every £8 you pay, the government adds £2, up to £2,000 a year per child (£4,000 if disabled). To claim free childcare you need a National Insurance number and a status that gives you access (for example, settled or pre-settled status).

5
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Say it aloud: “I'd like to apply for Child Benefit.”.
